waiver: harness-limit
reason: internal/interp has no allocator to count calls into — it is a
  tree-walking evaluator over Go values — so __heap_alloc_count()
  returns 0 there unconditionally and the shape this case measures is
  unobservable, exactly as for __heap_bump_bytes in
  alloc_flat_under_reclaim. Giving the interpreter a fake counter would
  make it report a number that describes nothing; see
  docs/ALLOCATION-OBSERVABLE.md.
